Arithmetica4 — Attribution & Provenance Notice

1. Mathlib4
   This project builds on Mathlib4 (https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4),
   rev 0df444a360eaa60ab8c11dca51a86af692955474, released under the Apache License 2.0.

2. Local & Global Class Field Theory (`RHDirect/Stage13CFT_IdeleNormResidue.lean`
   and `RHDirect/CFT_*.lean`)
   The 15 standalone Local & Global Class Field Theory, Ray Class Field, and Hilbert
   Class Field modules were extracted, consolidated, and adapted to targeted Mathlib
   imports (without `import Mathlib`) from the public `GroundTheory` formalization
   released in Levent Alpöge's Lean 4 archive. All credit for the original Lean 4
   proof architecture of `GroundTheory` belongs to its original author(s).

3. Bounded Prime Gaps (`PrimeGaps/`, `PrimeGapsTheory/`, and `PrimeGapsCert/`)
   Vendored unmodified from AxiomMath/PrimeGapsLib
   (https://github.com/AxiomMath/PrimeGapsLib),
   Copyright 2026 Axiom Math — Licensed under the Apache License 2.0.
   The Bombieri-Vinogradov hypothesis in `PrimeGapsLib` is discharged unconditionally
   by `MaynardDock/BombieriVinogradovAdapter.lean` from `RHDirect.Stage11BombieriVinogradov`,
   yielding `MaynardDock/Capstone246.lean` (`H = 246`).

4. PrimeNumberTheoremAnd
   Depends on `nil-commits/PrimeNumberTheoremAnd` (rev 6c89d5699e16114be6ec6f1b4ae48818a5ec8cc3,
   a public fork of `AxiomMath/PrimeNumberTheoremAnd` applying a 1-line Lean v4.33.1
   compatibility fix in `MediumPNT.lean`).

5. Soundness Transparency
   Please consult `docs/SOUNDNESS_AUDIT.md` for an exact, line-cited classification
   of every theorem in this repository into:
     - Tier A: Unconditional on native Mathlib types (0 extra hypotheses, 0 proxies)
     - Tier B: Conditional reductions / partial campaigns (explicit hypotheses)
     - Tier C: Legacy baseline proxy or toy models preserved for compatibility

6. Arithmetica4 Extensions & Prize Campaign Modules (`RHDirect/Arith4Ext_*`, `RHDirect/PPL*`, `Prize/*`)
   All 99 merged modules (`22` `RHDirect/Arith4Ext_*.lean` Tier A library engines,
   `59` `RHDirect/PPL*.lean` prize-problem & milestone modules, and `18` `Prize/*.lean`
   modules covering PPL 024, PPL 086, and PPL 176) are original Lean 4 (v4.33.1)
   formalizations written from scratch on targeted Mathlib imports, verified with
   official `leanchecker` and exhaustive `Lean.collectAxioms` (`0` sorry, `0` custom
   axioms). See `docs/EXTENSIONS_CATALOG.md` and `docs/PRIZE_CAMPAIGN_CATALOG.md`.
